item.description:
We’re looking for a process engineer with 5+ years of experience in scaling catalytic technologies to pilot and beyond. You will play a central role in designing, constructing, and commissioning our pilot unit and subsequently designing our first commercial unit. 

Required core competencies:

  - Procuring, integrating, operating, and fixing pilot-scale equipment; 
  - Pilot chemical plant commissioning and operation;
  - Experience with recycling loops;
  - Experience with gas-to-liquids processes (syngas-to-methanol preferred);
  - Collaboration with EPCs in overseeing FOAK commercial unit design;
  - Experience with Aspen or other process simulation software.

Preferred qualifications:

  - PLC/SCADA design and integration;
  - Experience working with modular systems; 
  - Experience working in a fast-paced startup environment.

As Rise Reforming scales, this role is expected to grow into a VP of Engineering or Chief Engineer position, leading a team of process and project engineers across multiple commercial deployments. Senior Chemical Process Engineer will report to the CTO.

Compensation: $125,000+/year + stock options + performance bonus + benefits (health insurance, 401k).

Location: In person, Chicago, IL and Wheaton, IL.

Must have a car.
